description.narrative:
The project aims to establish and exchange multi-disciplinary knowledge for a strengthening of sustainable aquaculture practices in ASEAN, building on available and relevant experience within ASEAN and from Norway, thereby contributing to ASEAN Member States’ (AMS) enhanced ability to adapt to changes or stresses caused by climate change.
The key project outcomes include:
1.	Increased awareness built among AMS on status, gaps, and opportunities for a Norway-ASEAN collaboration on sustainable aquaculture;
2.	Technical capacity and knowledge on environmental sustainability in aquaculture built amongst strategically important organizations and relevant companies in AMS;
3.	Capacity increased amongst ASEAN partners to assess the socioeconomic effects of different near-future production scenarios.

The main objetive is to support the effective implementation of strategic priorities in ASEAN’s Blue Economy Framework among the ASEAN member states, targeting policy and decision makers within public and private sectors as well as research institutes and organisations. Throughout the project – and reflected in the project outcomes – emphasis is put on strengthening capacity and increasing awareness among local government, private companies, and other relevant stakeholders within the region.
